-- Demo reviews.
 'An envoy on a frozen planet whose people have no fixed gender. The slow build of trust between Genly Ai and Estraven carries the book, and the crossing of the ice is one of the best sustained sequences in the genre.', 'Sam'),
('Project Hail Mary', 'Andy Weir', 'Science Fiction', 4,
 'Fun problem-solving science fiction with a lot of heart. Rocky is a great character. The amnesia device gets a bit mechanical by the end.', 'Priya'),
('Piranesi', 'Susanna Clarke', 'Fantasy', 5,
 'Short, strange and beautiful. The house of endless halls is described so precisely it feels real, and the reveal is handled with restraint.', 'Sam'),
('The Road', 'Cormac McCarthy', 'Literary Fiction', 4,
 'Bleak and spare. The father and son dialogue is stripped to almost nothing and it works. Hard to read, harder to forget.', 'Alex'),
('Educated', 'Tara Westover', 'Memoir', 4,
 'Growing up in a survivalist family in Idaho and getting to Cambridge with no formal schooling. Gripping, though some of the later chapters drag.', 'Priya'),
('The Thursday Murder Club', 'Richard Osman', 'Mystery', 3,
 'Cosy and charming but the plot is thin and there are too many point-of-view switches. Joyce''s diary entries are the highlight.', 'Alex');


